findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config loading tests and implementation don't distinguish NotFound from parse/permission
    errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer verified CWE-209: 'CliError::Display sanitizes output \u2014\
    \ ServerError Display doesn't expose internal message at error.rs:50'. TEA also\
    \ wrote tests for CWE-209 info leakage. However, the reviewer didn't flag that\
    \ eprintln! in main would still leak via Display since main.rs doesn't exist.\
    \ Partial catch \u2014 the sanitization exists but the stderr printing path wasn't\
    \ fully reviewed."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: ''tenant field is raw String, not TenantId
    newtype... axiathon-core exports TenantId. Both cli.rs:27 and client.rs:7 use
    raw strings. This defeats the type safety the project invested in building.'''
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies like clap_complete, comfy-table, csv,
    dirs, reqwest, toml use direct version strings instead of workspace = true.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: 'Config silently ignores unknown fields\
    \ \u2014 no deny_unknown_fields. A config file with token = \"secret\" silently\
    \ ignores the token key... typos like timout = 60 will be silently ignored.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in the test suite. TEA wrote the tests but the logical flaw wasn't caught
    by any phase.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with 'let _ = config'. TEA wrote config tests but this specific test's lack of
    assertions wasn't flagged.
